[[0,1347254,0,5,0,5,"2016-10-15T00:55:03","hansbrinker","",[],"","Why Is Diego Garcia Wall-To-Wall US Bombers? Have The US NeoCon Pentagon Maniacs Already Decided To Bomb The Syrian Army And Dare Russia To Start WW3?","http://www.rense.com/general96/diego.htm","NewsOne"],[1,6567339,0,1,1,0,"2016-10-15T01:47:51","pizza_mine","",[],"<p>No, Diego is a perfect place to position bombers. They can hit the middle eastern trouble spots while scaring the Chinese and their unnecessary agreesion in the sea of China.</p>"],[1,6567564,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-15T02:23:38","jobes","",[],"<p>If the goal was to get more bombers in position for Syria, then they should put them at the <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incirlik_Air_Base\">Incirlik Air Base</a> in Turkey. This definitely feels like they're gearing up for something much larger.</p>"],[1,6569112,0,0,0,0,"2016-10-15T08:44:22","elgindelta","",[],"<p>Not a chance. The deployed su-300 and 400 anti air batteries are already in place along with the supposed prototype su-500. Syrian airspace is locked up by the flick of a switch.</p>"]]
